<title>SRI LANKA: S.Lanka Vanik soars on merger.</title>
<headline>S.Lanka Vanik soars on merger.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of investment bank Vanik Inc rose  12 percent or 2.50 rupees to 23.50, in early Friday trade on news  of its merger with Forbes Ceylon Ltd, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The share is rising on retail buying, after news of the merger, because  small investors expect the relationship (merger) to improve profits  of both firms,&quot; said a local broker.</p>
<p>Vanik said on Thursday, it was negotiating with Global Equity Corporation  to buy the Canadian firm's 50 percent stake in Forbes Ceylon's issued  capital of 240 million shares.</p>
<p>---Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
